text.en:
Provide wall finishes that are installed over suitable substrates, use approved materials, follow required alignment/layout and achieve the specified appearance and durability.
This can include:
wall tile;
panels;
acoustic panels;
wall protection;
laminates;
specialty wall systems.

This differs slightly from exterior-envelope sealants because interior architectural sealants may be used for:
acoustic control;
sanitary joints;
finish joints;
movement joints;
perimeter sealing.
Install compatible sealant systems with correct joint preparation, geometry, adhesion and finish while maintaining the intended acoustic, sanitary or movement function.

This is intentionally flexible because Hochelaga may include systems we haven't yet seen.
Examples:
epoxy wall systems;
protective wall panels;
FRP panels;
acoustic treatments;
anti-static flooring;
industrial coatings;
specialty ceiling/wall systems.
Ensure specialty finishes are installed from approved products and mock-ups using the manufacturer/project-defined substrate preparation, sequencing and inspection criteria.
